{title: Come, Thou Almighty King}
{artist: Anonymous (attr. Charles Wesley) / Felice de Giardini}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening}
{key: G}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 3/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The United Methodist Hymnal (Nashville, Tennessee: United Methodist Publishing House, 1989), # 61)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Come, Thou al[Am]might[D]y [G]King,
[G]Help us Thy [D7]name [G]to [D7]sing,
[D7]Help us to praise!
[D7]Father all [G]glorious,
[D7]O’er all vic[G]torious,
[G]Come and reign over us,
[Am]Ancient [D7]of [G]Days!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Jesus, our [Am]Lord, [D]a[G]rise,
[G]Scatter our [D7]en[G]e[D7]mies,
[D7]And make them fall;
[D7]Let Thine al[G]mighty aid
[D7]Our sure de[G]fense be made,
[G]Our souls on Thee be stayed;
[Am]Lord, hear [D7]our [G]call.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Come, Thou in[Am]car[D]nate [G]Word,
[G]Gird on Thy [D7]might[G]y [D7]sword,
[D7]Our prayer attend!
[D7]Come, and Thy [G]people bless,
[D7]And give Thy [G]Word success,
[G]Spirit of holiness,
[Am]On us [D7]des[G]cend!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Come, holy [Am]Com[D]fort[G]er,
[G]Thy sacred [D7]wit[G]ness [D7]bear
[D7]In this glad hour.
[D7]Thou who al[G]mighty art,
[D7]Now rule in [G]every heart,
[G]And ne’er from us depart,
[Am]Spirit [D7]of [G]power!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G]To Thee, great [Am]One [D]in [G]Three,
[G]Eternal [D7]prais[G]es [D7]be,
[D7]Hence, evermore.
[D7]Thy sovereign [G]majesty
[D7]May we in [G]glory see,
[G]And to eternity
[Am]Love and [D7]a[G]dore!
{end_of_verse}
